data
  title JOIN vs IN for one-to-many fan-out
  desc 50 orders × 20 line items — IN sends one extra query but ships zero duplicated rows
  compares
    - label JOIN — 1 query
      children
        - label 1 round-trip
          desc Parent and child merged into one result set
        - label 1,000 rows returned
          desc 50 orders × 20 line items, all rows merged
        - label 950 rows are duplicate
          desc Order columns repeat once per child row
        - label Best for 1:1 or small fan-out
          desc Wins when parents have 1–5 children
    - label IN — 2 queries
      children
        - label 2 round-trips
          desc Fetch orders, then children WHERE id IN (...)
        - label 1,050 rows, zero duplication
          desc 50 order rows + 1,000 line-item rows, each once
        - label No repeated parent data
          desc ORM parses every row exactly once
        - label Best for heavy 1:many fan-out
          desc 10–1000 items, avoids result-set bloat
